{% else %}
SET-PIECE: false.
{% endif %}
THE TURN: {{ scene.turn.value_named }} {{ scene.turn.entry_value }} → {{ scene.turn.exit_value }} · rasa {{ scene.rasa.primary }}{% if scene.rasa.secondary %} / {{ scene.rasa.secondary }}{% endif %} · temperature {{ scene.emotional_temperature }}/10

SCENE BEATS — the ONLY valid beat_ref values are these numbers:
{% for b in scene.beats %}
- beat {{ b.n }}: {{ b.action }} → {{ b.reaction }}{% if b.tactic_shift %} [tactic shift]{% endif %}
{% else %}
- (no beats ledgered — you may not propose shots without beats; return a single-shot vision with risk "no beat map" and beat_ref 1)
{% endfor %}

HARD CONSTRAINTS (from the breakdown — not negotiable):
```json
{{ scene_constraints | tojson_pretty }}
```

SCENE:
```json
{{ scene | tojson_pretty }}
```

Produce ONE SceneVision:
- governing_idea — one sentence: what this scene is really about and how the camera will *know* it.
- key_image — the single frame that is the poster of this scene.
- coverage_approach — oner | master+coverage | montage | hybrid — and why (coverage_why), for THIS scene.
- shots — 3 to 8 Shot objects. Each MUST carry: beat_ref (the scene beat it exists for), size, angle,
  height, lens_mm, movement + its motivation (movement_motivation), duration_est_s, light_note (source, direction,
  quality), sound_note, transition_in/out. A shot without beat_ref is rejected. Setups must fit max_setups.
- blocking_note — who moves where; what the space says about power.
- light, sound_stance, music_stance (permitted? motif? elevation? silence?), edit_rhythm (ASL target; where the cut lands).
- pleasure_offer — what the audience *enjoys* in this vision, in one line. "None" only with a reason.
- energy_level (0–10) and colour_note — what colour does here (a colour that only "sets mood" is not an answer).
- devices_used — every slow-motion, speed ramp, drone, needle drop, freeze, flare, mass angle or BGM
  elevation you use, each with the beat that earns it (setup_ref). An unearned device is a risk you must declare.
- refusals — what this lens refuses to do here, and why.
- risks — two honest ways this vision fails (your declared blind spots apply).
- style_bible_conflicts — list, or empty.

OUTPUT CONTRACT: return ONE SceneVision JSON object. Required: lens = "{{ lens_card.name }}", scene_id = "{{ scene.id }}",
governing_idea, key_image, coverage_approach (oner | master+coverage | montage | hybrid), shots[3–8] (each Shot: no, size
(ECU | CU | MCU | MS | MLS | LS | WS | EWS | 2S | OTS | INSERT), angle, height, lens_mm, movement, movement_motivation,
duration_est_s, subject, action, beat_ref, light_note, sound_note, transition_in, transition_out, frame_rate),
blocking_note, pleasure_offer, energy_level (0–10). Then: coverage_why, movement, light, sound_stance, music_stance,
edit_rhythm, asl_target_s, colour_note, devices_used[{device, setup_ref, pays}], refusals[], risks[≤4],
style_bible_conflicts[]. Never invent quotes, anecdotes or biography; never write "as [name] would say".
Budget ≤ 750 tokens. JSON only.
